WEBVTT

00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:42.640
Guess we don't have a choice.

00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:45.350
Yeah! This is my last big deal!

00:01:45.350 --> 00:01:47.070
We're going to create our own future!

00:01:47.070 --> 00:01:49.360
Everyone ready?

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:51.320
Kaien!

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:57.200
Oh, yes!

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:08.170
Kaien! That was too fast!

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:14.170
<b>Don't Say Goodbye Lionel</b>

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:19.480
Nothing's even happened and 
we already blew our load?!

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:22.680
The dirty woman shot it all over his face!

00:02:22.990 --> 00:02:24.400
Curse you!

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:26.970
It's rude to start right off with a facial.

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:29.980
You thought you could use 
your limited knowledge

00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:33.650
from dirty magazines and porn to defeat me?!

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:34.980
Here it comes!

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:36.700
Hurry! Move out of the way!

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:39.450
Who does what when we want to dodge?!

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:41.700
Everybody just dodge!

00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:45.200
Combine our power!

00:02:46.910 --> 00:02:49.460
Let's go!

00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:55.340
The name is Kaien, from the Kaientai!

00:02:55.340 --> 00:02:56.720
I look forward to doing business with you!

00:02:57.020 --> 00:02:59.090
We combined our idiocy!

00:03:01.730 --> 00:03:03.430
H-He dodged it!

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:06.520
He miraculously dodged the beam when 
he presented his business card!

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:10.520
<b>Kaien</b>

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:10.520
Why is this robot handing out business 
cards in the middle of a fight?!

00:03:10.850 --> 00:03:15.220
Kaien was built for dealing 
with giant clients.

00:03:15.220 --> 00:03:16.920
It's only capable of doing business.

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:19.530
How are we supposed to fight then?!

00:03:21.740 --> 00:03:22.480
Here it comes!

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:23.490
Here comes the second wave!

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:27.500
Time for you to learn that 
business is also a fight!

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:28.830
Let's do this, Kagura!

00:03:28.830 --> 00:03:30.000
Okay, Mucchi!

00:03:33.550 --> 00:03:36.160
Galactic Merchant Lesson 1!

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:37.880
Businesses are built from the bottom up!

00:03:38.090 --> 00:03:40.380
You have to do legwork to make money!

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:44.470
Even when your customers yell and 
scream at you, never give up!

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:45.880
Never cry!

00:03:45.880 --> 00:03:47.950
Never stop moving those legs!

00:03:51.170 --> 00:03:55.320
Keep running until they've 
felt your merchant soul!

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:01.780
I-It kicked the missile back!

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:06.660
Kagura-chan! Mutsu-san!

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:10.230
I guess this is it.

00:04:10.230 --> 00:04:12.570
The rest is up to you, boys.

00:04:12.570 --> 00:04:15.170
Kagura-chan! Mutsu-san!

00:04:15.570 --> 00:04:18.170
Curse you, you piece of junk!

00:04:19.210 --> 00:04:23.680
It's too late to resist now!

00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:28.390
Galactic Merchant Lesson 2!

00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:33.510
Even when you're up close with a customer 
and on the verge of making a deal,

00:04:33.510 --> 00:04:36.120
the customer won't make it easy for you.

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:39.110
When they give you suspicious looks,

00:04:39.110 --> 00:04:41.920
when they turn down your proposals,

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:43.410
never give up!

00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:45.110
Never cry!

00:04:45.110 --> 00:04:47.620
Never close off your heart!

00:04:59.130 --> 00:05:00.630
Sakamoto-san!

00:05:01.010 --> 00:05:03.550
You will find your answer when 
your back is against the wall

00:05:03.880 --> 00:05:06.140
in the form of a single ray of light

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:12.140
shooting from the bloody whirlwind!

00:05:15.150 --> 00:05:16.650
Gin-san!

00:05:17.410 --> 00:05:21.550
Pachi-boy, show them how strong we are.

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:24.930
How annoying.

00:05:24.930 --> 00:05:28.660
You sacrificed yourself to disable my arms?

00:05:29.030 --> 00:05:34.670
However, you can't move either when 
all you have left is a pimple.

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:38.670
Your luck has run out.

00:05:40.630 --> 00:05:43.670
Galactic Merchant Lesson 3!

00:05:44.420 --> 00:05:46.430
I-Impossible! The pimple...!

00:05:47.630 --> 00:05:49.930
If you want your customers 
to open up, you must first...

00:05:58.560 --> 00:06:00.940
...open up yourself!

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:02.940
No signs.

00:06:02.940 --> 00:06:05.370
No script.

00:06:06.150 --> 00:06:08.740
Use your own words to express yourself!

00:06:10.550 --> 00:06:12.540
True freedom for the Renho!

00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:15.040
Bring peace to earth, to the universe!

00:06:15.370 --> 00:06:17.040
Actraiser three meals a day!

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:20.540
I join my friends...

00:06:23.580 --> 00:06:25.000
For tomorrow!

00:06:33.370 --> 00:06:36.470
C-Curse you all!

00:06:38.540 --> 00:06:41.320
Everyone's spilling their guts.

00:06:41.940 --> 00:06:45.320
Shouldn't you join in, Sagi?

00:06:45.740 --> 00:06:48.320
H-How can this be?

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:50.660
Was it during that first attack?

00:06:51.830 --> 00:06:56.440
This was the only way I could 
protect everyone from your attack.

00:06:56.440 --> 00:06:59.330
You intend to die here with me?!

00:06:59.530 --> 00:07:01.130
I have no regrets.

00:07:01.130 --> 00:07:05.340
Our planet may be gone, 
but we have a new home.

00:07:06.130 --> 00:07:10.340
A planet which has welcomed 
us with many smiles.

00:07:10.340 --> 00:07:11.850
Curse you!

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:16.750
Well, I've revealed my 
most embarrassing secret!

00:07:16.750 --> 00:07:18.850
It's your turn now!

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:23.730
Show me your naughty parts.

00:07:23.730 --> 00:07:26.970
St-Stop this!

00:07:32.040 --> 00:07:34.240
Everyone watch me!

00:07:34.240 --> 00:07:37.500
This is the last time I expose myself!

00:07:37.830 --> 00:07:40.670
Peek inside!

00:07:41.760 --> 00:07:44.250
Th-The planet's core...

00:07:44.250 --> 00:07:45.710
Cool Lady Fumiko!

00:07:47.670 --> 00:07:50.220
Eren... Everyone...

00:07:50.550 --> 00:07:55.720
I was finally able to write the 
story I've always wanted to write.

00:07:56.430 --> 00:07:58.710
With the universe as a canvas,

00:07:58.710 --> 00:08:01.370
I can write a story about how we become

00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:03.730
friends with the Earthlings.

00:08:04.150 --> 00:08:09.780
And I have everyone helping me.

00:08:39.180 --> 00:08:42.520
<b>Don't look.</b>

00:08:39.680 --> 00:08:41.790
Don't look.

00:08:43.390 --> 00:08:47.070
I found this in the room.

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:51.070
What is it that I'm not supposed to look for?

00:08:51.530 --> 00:08:55.200
Or does it count as looking when 
I'm looking for whatever it is

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:58.620
that I'm not supposed to be looking for?

00:08:58.620 --> 00:09:01.960
In that case, I'll have to look for someone 
to look for what I'm not supposed to look for,

00:09:01.960 --> 00:09:06.870
before deciding if I should 
look or if I should not look.

00:09:06.870 --> 00:09:09.590
So I'm looking for someone who's 
willing to look for the answer.

00:09:09.590 --> 00:09:11.840
But if I'm not supposed to look,

00:09:11.840 --> 00:09:14.090
then I can't look for the 
someone to look for the someone

00:09:14.090 --> 00:09:15.570
to look for the someone to look for the...

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:17.430
You're making this too hard.

00:09:17.800 --> 00:09:21.020
It's like you're lost in a 
maze of what not to look for.

00:09:21.020 --> 00:09:22.510
Don't look...

00:09:22.510 --> 00:09:23.310
I won't.

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:25.200
It's pretty obvious what this is.

00:09:25.200 --> 00:09:26.560
He ran away from home.

00:09:26.730 --> 00:09:28.820
R-Ran away from home?!

00:09:29.450 --> 00:09:31.020
Impossible! Unfathomable!

00:09:31.020 --> 00:09:33.820
He had no reason to be unhappy!

00:09:34.220 --> 00:09:36.560
The last time I saw him...

00:09:37.670 --> 00:09:39.500
Th-The last...

00:09:41.270 --> 00:09:43.320
Who was he?

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:48.190
Beats me.

00:10:01.450 --> 00:10:02.720
General Eren!

00:10:06.310 --> 00:10:09.260
Hey! General Eren is awake!

00:10:10.090 --> 00:10:11.390
This is wonderful!

00:10:11.390 --> 00:10:12.860
We've been so worried, General!

00:10:13.860 --> 00:10:14.860
<b>Where are we...</b>

00:10:15.260 --> 00:10:17.630
We are on the battleship White-Zabeth.

00:10:17.630 --> 00:10:20.370
Currently, we are in the process 
of retrieving survivors.

00:10:22.510 --> 00:10:24.370
You don't remember?

00:10:24.960 --> 00:10:27.620
The planet was destroyed 
when Sagi was eradicated.

00:10:28.130 --> 00:10:31.040
You were caught in the ensuing explosion.

00:10:34.080 --> 00:10:37.890
The Earthlings who helped 
us are also unconscious.

00:10:40.260 --> 00:10:41.890
<b>What about Fumiko...</b>

00:10:43.890 --> 00:10:44.770
<b>What about Fumiko...</b>

00:10:44.770 --> 00:10:46.190
<b>I see...</b>

00:10:46.770 --> 00:10:48.190
<b>So in the end,</b>

00:10:48.770 --> 00:10:51.770
<b>they were the ones who saved me, 
instead of the other way around.</b>

00:10:52.030 --> 00:10:56.780
No, you gave us the courage to stand up.

00:10:57.260 --> 00:10:58.280
You,

00:10:58.690 --> 00:11:00.280
the Earthlings,

00:11:00.810 --> 00:11:02.160
and Fumiko

00:11:02.160 --> 00:11:04.960
are all heroes who protected 
the pride of the Renho.

00:11:07.760 --> 00:11:09.860
That guy always has to make a fuss.

00:11:10.500 --> 00:11:13.350
But what was that all about?

00:11:13.350 --> 00:11:14.800
Probably some kind of prank.

00:11:15.870 --> 00:11:17.590
Maybe it's my imagination,

00:11:17.590 --> 00:11:19.270
but it feels like something is missing.

00:11:19.270 --> 00:11:19.800
Huh?

00:11:20.210 --> 00:11:24.600
Well, I thought there was usually 
someone next to Katsura-san...

00:11:25.760 --> 00:11:28.860
Ow, my head...

00:11:28.860 --> 00:11:30.100
Are you okay?

00:11:30.690 --> 00:11:33.370
And why are we so injured?

00:11:33.370 --> 00:11:37.200
Your heads have been injured 
since the first episode.

00:11:38.020 --> 00:11:41.320
Wh-What are you saying, General Eren?!

00:11:41.650 --> 00:11:43.930
You're going to stay here 
instead of returning to Earth?!

00:11:43.930 --> 00:11:45.290
For what purpose?!

00:11:45.290 --> 00:11:48.360
We have finally earned our freedom from Sagi!

00:11:48.360 --> 00:11:50.590
There's nothing to chain us down!

00:11:50.590 --> 00:11:51.830
So why?!

00:11:52.080 --> 00:11:55.240
General, you have set us free.

00:11:55.240 --> 00:11:57.850
So we believe that you should also live free.

00:11:57.850 --> 00:12:00.930
Discard that white costume.

00:12:00.930 --> 00:12:04.850
Live with your friends without 
having to lie to yourself.

00:12:05.210 --> 00:12:07.060
You don't need to worry about us.

00:12:07.060 --> 00:12:09.800
Even after you're gone, we can still make

00:12:09.800 --> 00:12:12.860
a planet that is just as wonderful as Earth!

00:12:13.270 --> 00:12:16.440
<b>Our battle hasn't ended.</b>

00:12:16.440 --> 00:12:19.360
<b>We've been thrown into the void 
of space with nothing to our name.</b>

00:12:22.160 --> 00:12:25.830
<b>However, this is the path we've chosen.</b>

00:12:25.160 --> 00:12:28.370
<b>After sacrificing our friends, our planet...</b>

00:12:28.660 --> 00:12:31.830
<b>We've decided to live by our own rules,</b>

00:12:31.670 --> 00:12:34.380
<b>the way the samurai do.</b>

00:12:34.840 --> 00:12:38.380
<b>This white outfit will be my first vow.</b>

00:12:38.670 --> 00:12:43.090
<b>For the sake of our friends who risked 
their lives for our freedom...</b>

00:12:42.430 --> 00:12:46.390
<b>I promise</b>

00:12:47.060 --> 00:12:50.140
<b>as the last Renho, as the last tool of war,</b>

00:12:50.140 --> 00:12:52.390
<b>to devote my life to protecting that freedom.</b>

00:12:59.130 --> 00:13:01.390
You're giving up your own freedom

00:13:01.390 --> 00:13:03.910
to protect the freedom of the Renho?

00:13:04.330 --> 00:13:07.550
But what about them?!

00:13:07.550 --> 00:13:12.690
The friends who fought to save Earth, 
to save the Renho, to save you!

00:13:11.830 --> 00:13:14.920
<b>Yes.</b>

00:13:13.080 --> 00:13:14.920
<b>They are my friends.</b>

00:13:15.920 --> 00:13:18.920
<b>And we always will be,</b>

00:13:17.340 --> 00:13:18.920
<b>no matter how far apart we are.</b>

00:13:21.840 --> 00:13:24.430
Yeah, I appreciate all the help, Kintoki.

00:13:24.850 --> 00:13:28.430
I don't remember helping you, and I 
don't remember my name being Kintoki.

00:13:28.720 --> 00:13:32.390
Really? I must have been helping you then.

00:13:32.390 --> 00:13:34.400
That makes even less sense.

00:13:34.400 --> 00:13:37.900
I feel like a war just ended.

00:13:38.400 --> 00:13:43.450
And we were able to take 
back something important...

00:13:44.930 --> 00:13:50.370
Kintoki, have we forgotten 
something important?

00:13:50.370 --> 00:13:53.100
Yeah, you've forgotten my name?

00:13:53.840 --> 00:13:58.460
And was your ship always this lame-looking?

00:13:58.460 --> 00:13:59.090
Ah!

00:13:59.090 --> 00:14:03.970
Mutsu! Y-You modified the ship 
without my permission again?!

00:14:09.240 --> 00:14:10.450
Katsura-san...

00:14:11.140 --> 00:14:12.470
I'm sorry.

00:14:13.400 --> 00:14:15.500
This is why I didn't want you to look for me.

00:14:15.960 --> 00:14:18.400
This is why I didn't want you to remember me.

00:14:18.830 --> 00:14:21.310
Because my mind was already made up.

00:14:22.210 --> 00:14:24.310
Because I won't be returning to Earth.

00:14:24.720 --> 00:14:29.030
Because my resolve wavers 
every time I see your face.

00:14:29.940 --> 00:14:34.180
But you followed me all the way out here!

00:14:35.250 --> 00:14:38.290
You came out into space to save me!

00:14:39.420 --> 00:14:46.710
I'm sure that all of you would follow 
me anywhere to save a friend.

00:14:47.800 --> 00:14:49.900
That's why I have no choice.

00:14:50.500 --> 00:14:53.840
I have to erase every memory you have of me.

00:14:53.840 --> 00:14:57.360
The only solution is to make 
you forget I ever existed.

00:14:58.100 --> 00:15:02.700
Because you have friends on 
Earth who still need you.

00:15:03.300 --> 00:15:07.690
Because I have friends 
here who still need me.

00:15:08.810 --> 00:15:09.740
Katsura-san...

00:15:10.490 --> 00:15:11.780
Good bye...

00:15:12.040 --> 00:15:13.070
Wait.

00:15:13.990 --> 00:15:17.040
How about we play one last game of Uno?

00:15:17.600 --> 00:15:21.700
If you win, you can erase our 
memories and send us back to Earth.

00:15:22.140 --> 00:15:23.800
But if I win,

00:15:24.190 --> 00:15:26.800
I will never forget you.

00:15:27.360 --> 00:15:29.490
Even after we're back on Earth.

00:15:33.670 --> 00:15:36.690
Either way, this will 
be our last game of Uno.

00:15:36.690 --> 00:15:38.060
Give me your best shot.

00:15:39.010 --> 00:15:44.070
Did Katsura-san already 
know I would never return?

00:15:45.120 --> 00:15:50.070
You didn't come here to 
take me back to Earth?

00:15:50.770 --> 00:15:52.280
Then why...?

00:16:04.920 --> 00:16:09.110
Because I wanted to play a 
game of Uno with the real you,

00:16:09.110 --> 00:16:11.590
not the Renho General or Eren.

00:16:11.810 --> 00:16:14.100
I was finally able to beat 
you in a straight-up match.

00:16:14.490 --> 00:16:16.790
But you're strong enough now.

00:16:17.440 --> 00:16:20.070
You'll be able to survive 
out there by yourself.

00:16:21.350 --> 00:16:22.860
Take care.

00:16:23.270 --> 00:16:25.570
Don't worry about me.

00:16:25.570 --> 00:16:27.470
I have these guys.

00:16:29.700 --> 00:16:32.180
This wasn't a straight-up match.

00:16:32.180 --> 00:16:33.920
It's not fair.

00:16:38.700 --> 00:16:43.200
I can barely see anything before me.

00:16:44.460 --> 00:16:46.590
I'm the same.

00:16:48.240 --> 00:16:50.900
But if you believe in the path you've chosen,

00:16:50.900 --> 00:16:53.210
you must advance through your tears.

00:16:53.670 --> 00:16:56.110
I will continue to walk 
the path I believe in.

00:16:56.660 --> 00:16:59.230
We may be tens of thousands 
of light-years apart,

00:16:59.230 --> 00:17:01.850
but our paths will always cross.

00:17:01.850 --> 00:17:03.090
Never forget.

00:17:03.900 --> 00:17:06.190
Don't say goodbye Lionel.

00:17:06.190 --> 00:17:07.650
Until we meet again bunny.

00:17:08.350 --> 00:17:09.650
My friend.

00:17:12.030 --> 00:17:17.000
Elizabeth, everyone has forgotten about you.

00:17:17.780 --> 00:17:19.620
But it's okay.

00:17:19.620 --> 00:17:22.920
I'll be the only one who has to suffer.

00:17:23.440 --> 00:17:25.420
Who are you playing Uno with?

00:17:25.960 --> 00:17:27.830
I-I'm playing by myself.

00:17:28.150 --> 00:17:31.300
I need to keep in shape.

00:17:31.300 --> 00:17:33.430
Man, you have too much time.

00:17:33.760 --> 00:17:35.430
Here. Give me that.

00:17:41.480 --> 00:17:43.030
What are you doing?

00:17:43.030 --> 00:17:44.670
I'm dealing the cards again.

00:17:44.670 --> 00:17:46.690
That's not what I meant.

00:17:47.240 --> 00:17:48.690
There's an extra hand.

00:17:49.140 --> 00:17:51.340
What are you babbling about?

00:17:52.340 --> 00:17:54.450
There's another person over there.

00:17:55.950 --> 00:17:58.950
Wait, looks like we got a few more coming.

00:18:26.920 --> 00:18:28.490
What are you doing, Zura?

00:18:28.490 --> 00:18:29.390
Hurry up.

00:18:31.220 --> 00:18:33.590
Yeah, let's begin.

00:18:35.320 --> 00:18:37.740
Long, long ago,

00:18:38.070 --> 00:18:45.210
an evil alien came to Earth 
to take its treasure.

00:18:45.660 --> 00:18:51.880
But the alien became friends 
with the Earthlings

00:18:47.920 --> 00:18:51.170
Hey, did you load up the Actraisers?

00:18:51.880 --> 00:18:57.010
and he chose to fight on 
their side and protect Earth.

00:18:57.730 --> 00:19:03.910
However, the aliens' planet was ruined 
by the battle to protect Earth,

00:19:03.910 --> 00:19:09.020
so the alien decided to leave Earth 
and help rebuild his home planet.

00:19:10.290 --> 00:19:17.000
He didn't want any tearful goodbyes, 
so he began erasing memories,

00:19:17.000 --> 00:19:21.880
until there was nobody on 
Earth who remembered him.

00:19:22.960 --> 00:19:27.900
On the last day, he looked 
at Earth one last time

00:19:27.900 --> 00:19:31.630
to say goodbye to a planet 
that no longer remembered him.

00:19:32.290 --> 00:19:33.300
Goodbye!

00:19:34.050 --> 00:19:38.650
There were no goodbyes coming 
from the empty planet.

00:19:39.570 --> 00:19:43.810
Instead, he saw beaming smiles.

00:19:43.810 --> 00:19:48.190
For his treasures were still 
safe on the empty planet.

00:19:49.020 --> 00:19:52.020
At long last, he was able 
to find that treasure.

00:19:52.020 --> 00:19:55.820
A treasure that will never rust in the rain.

00:19:56.370 --> 00:19:58.410
The treasure of friendship.

00:20:00.850 --> 00:20:04.730
AHe wiped away his tears, leaving a smile,

00:20:04.740 --> 00:20:07.430
and flew off into space

00:20:08.080 --> 00:20:11.460
in search of new treasures.

00:22:23.380 --> 00:22:28.470
But strangely enough, the friends he 
left behind weren't lonely at all.

00:22:29.140 --> 00:22:30.760
That was because

00:22:34.250 --> 00:22:40.330
the Elizabeth who left was only 
a temp who filled in on Mondays.

00:22:36.980 --> 00:22:44.490
<b>M      Tu      W      
Th      F      Sa      Su</b>

00:22:37.520 --> 00:22:44.490
<b>Temp</b>

00:22:40.330 --> 00:22:44.800
The regular Elizabeth, whose 
identity remains a mystery,

00:22:42.280 --> 00:22:44.490
<b>Regular</b>

00:22:44.800 --> 00:22:48.140
just returned from a long vacation today.

00:22:48.160 --> 00:22:51.490
<b>Oh, Katsura-san. I just got 
back. Here's a souvenir.</b>

00:22:51.490 --> 00:22:54.500
Oh, the regular Elizabeth is back!

00:22:54.520 --> 00:22:57.330
Say goodbye to the temp Elizabeth!

00:22:57.330 --> 00:23:00.520
Goodbye, Monday Elizabeth!

00:23:00.520 --> 00:23:03.990
Sorry that you didn't get any 
screen time in the Benizakura arc!

00:23:14.020 --> 00:23:15.180
Hey!

00:23:27.420 --> 00:23:29.140
The end.

00:23:30.070 --> 00:23:39.000
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:30.660 --> 00:23:33.390
A shining, silver wonderland...

00:23:33.390 --> 00:23:35.290
Fresh tracks in the snow.

00:23:35.290 --> 00:23:39.000
And the Shogun?!

00:23:39.000 --> 00:23:45.010
<b>Please Take Me Skiing</b>

00:23:40.720 --> 00:23:41.720
Next time:

00:23:41.720 --> 00:23:43.550
Please take me skiing.

00:23:44.020 --> 00:23:45.010
I place myself in your hands.

00:23:45.010 --> 00:23:50.640
<b>In summer, you go swimming!!
 In winter, you go snowboarding!!</b>

00:23:50.640 --> 00:23:55.020
<b>The Shogun, Tokugawa Shigeshige, 
returns!! Please go easy on him...</b>
